Z||000000||Deer_Slayer||03-14-2000||11:22 AM||||So far, work on the 86 notchback has come a long way.  Here is sort of a timeline of it's progress:<P>  November 99: car aquired and put into    <BR>               storage.<BR>  Christmas Eve, 99: coupe brought home and <BR>               given to my stepdad.<BR>  Dec 27: washed for the first time.<BR>  Dec 28: oil and tranny fluid change,new<BR>               pan gasket. <BR>  Dec 30: Junkyard raid.  Car received ash-<BR>               trays, 5 stock lugnuts, wheel<BR>               center cap, horn button.  <BR>               First waxing and quad pipes<BR>               polished.  <BR>  Jan 2000: missing lugnut caps replaced.  <BR>              new shocks, new bushings,<BR>              new struts and housings.<BR>              replacement sail pannels <BR>              ordered from kick hill <BR>              farm.  <BR>  Feb 2000: new ball joints,  new tires,<BR>              passenger side rocker pannel<BR>              replaced.  Emergency brake<BR>              locked up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> , replaced. <BR>  March:  now sits outside while repairs on<BR>             the house occur.<P>        Still to be done:<P>  -replace cracked rear view mirror.<BR>  -replace cracked sail pannels.<BR>  -buff wheels.<BR>  -other mishelaneous details.<P>  I'll try my best to get the car in perfect shape by summer.||||reg||1
